  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Consider the functions\n$$\\begin{aligned}f(x)&=2^x-1,\\\\g(x)&=2^{-x}+2.\\end{aligned}$$\nFind the range of each of the following functions:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q10a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f\\circ g$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(3,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "The range of $g$ is $(2,\\infty)$, and $f$ is increasing.\n$$\\begin{align*}(f\\circ g)(x)&=2^{g(x)}-1,\\\\(f\\circ g)(x)&>2^2-1=3.\\end{align*}$$\nThe lower endpoint is a limit, and there is no upper bound. The range is $(3,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q10b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$g\\circ f$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2,4)$.",
          "worked": "The range of $f$ is $(-1,\\infty)$. Thus\n$$\\begin{align*}(g\\circ f)(x)&=2^{-f(x)}+2,\\\\-f(x)&<1,\\\\0&<2^{-f(x)}<2,\\\\2&<(g\\circ f)(x)<4.\\end{align*}$$\nNeither endpoint is attained. The range is $(2,4)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q10c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f\\circ f$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-\\tfrac12,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "The range of $f$ is $(-1,\\infty)$, and $f$ is increasing.\n$$\\begin{align*}(f\\circ f)(x)&=2^{f(x)}-1,\\\\(f\\circ f)(x)&>2^{-1}-1=-\\tfrac12.\\end{align*}$$\nThe lower endpoint is excluded and the values are unbounded above. The range is $(-\\tfrac12,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q10d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$g\\circ g$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2,\\tfrac94)$.",
          "worked": "The range of $g$ is $(2,\\infty)$. Hence\n$$\\begin{align*}(g\\circ g)(x)&=2^{-g(x)}+2,\\\\-g(x)&<-2,\\\\0&<2^{-g(x)}<\\tfrac14,\\\\2&<(g\\circ g)(x)<\\tfrac94.\\end{align*}$$\nNeither endpoint is attained. The range is $(2,\\tfrac94)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      }
    ]
  },
